From ddda4cf634503dd9ce8948bd7121b475dd12a810 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AaravSai Anugula <aaravsai.anugula@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 18:59:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] sato: expose @opencode-ai/app/entry so wrapper can reuse
 upstream entry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Files touched (upstream):
  - packages/app/package.json (+1)   add "./entry" export to package.json exports

Why:
  packages/sato-app is a THIN wrapper around @opencode-ai/app that applies the
  Sato skin (CSS override + title + favicon + data-theme default) around the
  same UI. Without an export for the entry, the wrapper had to hand-copy
  upstream packages/app/src/entry.tsx and re-implement Platform / notify /
  ServerConnection / auth-token URL flow — every upstream change to that
  entry then has to be mirrored by hand.

  Adding a single "./entry" export lets the wrapper import upstream's entry
  as-is and inject only the Sato skin, eliminating the drift risk and the
  three regressions the hand-copy introduced (dropped auth_token URL flow,
  dropped notification onclick, hardcoded "sato" version string).

Owner: sato-code fork maintainers (@aaravsaianugula)
Kill-criterion: delete when upstream OpenCode ships this export itself
  (a one-line PR upstream would collapse this patch to zero).
---
 packages/app/package.json | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/app/package.json b/packages/app/package.json
index 7430a614b..e3f93078b 100644
--- a/packages/app/package.json
+++ b/packages/app/package.json
@@ -9,7 +9,8 @@
     "./updater": "./src/updater.ts",
     "./wsl/types": "./src/wsl/types.ts",
     "./vite": "./vite.js",
-    "./index.css": "./src/index.css"
+    "./index.css": "./src/index.css",
+    "./entry": "./src/entry.tsx"
   },
   "scripts": {
     "typecheck": "tsgo -b",
-- 
2.54.0.windows.1

